@startuml

title The registration of a first external sign-in

skinparam activityDiamondBackgroundColor #F7F7F7

start
:a validated ID token names an issuer and a subject;
if (a live link names that pair?) then (yes)
    :the account the link names is the one that signs in;
else (no)
    :the registration policy decides the tenant,
    the party and the default role;
    note right
      The same policy a password sign-up
      goes through: one place decides what a
      new account receives, whatever door it
      came through.
    end note
    :an account is created as a first sign-in;
    :a link from that issuer and subject to it is written;
endif
:a session is opened, its method the provider that proved it;
stop

@enduml
